            - Guards: production's first-contact reds are recorded and classified, held-out seeds pass, and a sample of
              the model's expectations is read by a different model family (Fable).
            - Store (wide consult Q4 A): `Store` is its own service with `load` (a typed failure) and one atomic
              `write(batch)` with no `purpose` or `acknowledges`, shipped as `layerMemory`; one batch stream per
              Runtime, so an awaited acknowledgement carries everything dirty (WriteAhead R10); the disk reader
              derives purpose and acknowledgement from bytes.
            - Host (wide consult W2): `Page` replaces `Host`'s visibility, the seed comes from `effect/Crypto`, and
              storage is read and validated in a layer built before any app service (Actors I4, a case red first).
            - Edge (W2): a pure `edgeStep(state, input)` with a tagged state (`Clean`, `Waiting`, `Out`) replaces
              `edge.ts`'s flags; its runner only writes and sleeps, and the crash gate enumerates its states.
